<header><p class="st-kicker">tribal confederation · Egypt, North Africa and Sudan</p><h1 class="st-title">Iwellemmeden Kel Ataram</h1><p class="st-meta">1650 CE – 1916 CE (approx.) · capital Menaka</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The western Iwellemmeden Tuareg confederation, which dominated the Niger Bend around Menaka and led a major revolt against the French in 1916.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iwellemmeden">Iwellemmeden</a> were a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tuareg">Tuareg</a> confederation that moved into the region east of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/niger-bend">Niger Bend</a> in the 17th century, filling the vacuum after the fall of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/songhai-empire">Songhai Empire</a> and the weakening of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/pashalik-of-timbuktu">Pashalik of Timbuktu</a>. In the 18th century they divided into the western Kel Ataram and the eastern <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/iwellemmeden-kel-dinnik">Iwellemmeden Kel Dinnik</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The Kel Ataram were led by an amenokal, the paramount chief, drawn from a noble lineage. Noble warriors controlled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassal</a> herders, dependent farmers along the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/niger-river">Niger</a> and enslaved people. They raided and taxed the Songhai-speaking riverine communities and controlled pastures around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/menaka">Menaka</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/azawagh">Azawagh</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> occupied the region around 1900. In 1916 the amenokal <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/firhun-ag-alinsar">Firhun ag Alinsar</a> launched a revolt during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a>; he was defeated and killed later that year, and the confederation's power was broken.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="tribal confederation, 1650 CE – 1916 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><ellipse cx="44" cy="56" rx="16" ry="24"/><path d="M44 34 V78"/><path d="M68 20 V84"/><path d="M68 20 L63 30 H73 Z"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">tribal confederation</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Egypt, North Africa and Sudan</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:92.54%;width:5.29%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1650 CE – 1916 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>tribal confederation</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>nomadic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Menaka</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Firhun ag Alinsar</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Tamasheq (Tuareg)</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/mali">Mali</a>, <a href="/countries/niger">Niger</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Western Iwellemmeden, Ouelleminden Kel Ataram</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1783&amp;focus=iwellemmeden-kel-ataram" aria-label="Iwellemmeden Kel Ataram on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4625 1485 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Iwellemmeden Kel Ataram lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M4523 1888h0M5144 1880h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4945 1741h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M4945 1741h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day Mali. <a href="/atlas?year=1783&amp;focus=iwellemmeden-kel-ataram">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

